# deejay-cog — the names this cog reads. Names only: the values live in
# Doppler (deejay-cog / dev locally, prd deployed). Run under
# `doppler run -- …`; do not copy this to .env — nothing reads it.
#
# Uncommented names are required in Doppler's dev config, and
# `uv run check-doppler-keys` checks dev holds every one. Commented names
# are optional: the code has a default, only production reads them, or only
# one local-only flow needs them. How the deployed worker loads them, and
# what each part does when one is missing: docs/CONFIGURATION.md.

# ── API ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# external tooling: read by miniapppolis-common-utils' KaianoApiClient.
# Base URL of api-kaianolevine-com: production reads the unsuffixed name,
# every other environment the _DEV one, with no fallback between them.
# Unset, nothing is ingested and run reports are logged rather than sent.
KAIANO_API_BASE_URL_DEV=
# KAIANO_API_BASE_URL=
# This cog's own API key. The API attributes every call to deejay-cog by it;
# the shared client falls back to the generic KAIANO_API_KEY when it is
# unset, and with neither every call fails.
DEEJAY_COG_API_KEY=

# ── Google ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# external tooling: read by miniapppolis-common-utils' GoogleAPI.
# Service-account JSON for Drive and Sheets, on one line.
GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS_JSON=

# ── Spotify (all three credentials, or every Spotify step is skipped) ─────
# external tooling: the credentials and redirect URI are read by
# miniapppolis-common-utils' Spotify client. The refresh token is generated
# once (docs/SPOTIFY_SETUP.md); the redirect URI (default
# http://127.0.0.1:8888/callback) must match the Spotify dashboard.
SPOTIPY_CLIENT_ID=
SPOTIPY_CLIENT_SECRET=
SPOTIPY_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# SPOTIPY_REDIRECT_URI=
# The standing radio playlist. Unset, every synced set counts a Spotify
# failure.
SPOTIFY_RADIO_PLAYLIST_ID=

# ── Drive folders and behaviour ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The folder IDs default to the production folders in config.py: the drop
# zone process-new-files sweeps, the parent of the year folders and the
# Summary folder, and the VirtualDJ history folder ingest-live-history
# reads. Outside production, process-new-files refuses to run unless
# CSV_SOURCE_FOLDER_ID is set: point it at a test drop zone.
# CSV_SOURCE_FOLDER_ID=
# DJ_SETS_FOLDER_ID=
# VDJ_HISTORY_FOLDER_ID=
# Timezone live plays are stamped in, and the "today" the repair pass
# counts back from (default America/Chicago).
# TIMEZONE=
# Repair pass: how far back by set date it checks for a missing API set or
# Spotify playlist (default 183 days), and repairs per sweep (default 3).
# REPAIR_LOOKBACK_DAYS=
# REPAIR_MAX_PER_RUN=
# Production only: the fingerprint function's queue, where retag-music
# sends files with no usable title or artist. Unset, nothing is sent.
# DEEJAY_FINGERPRINT_QUEUE_URL=

# ── Observability and environment ─────────────────────────────────────────
# external tooling: read by miniapppolis-common-utils' environment module,
# init_sentry and logger. ENVIRONMENT: unset resolves to local; the Lambda
# sets production. SENTRY_DSN_COGS is read once per cold start.
# LOGGING_LEVEL defaults to INFO and is re-applied every invocation.
# ENVIRONMENT=
# SENTRY_DSN_COGS=
# LOGGING_LEVEL=

# ── Local-only flows ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# update-dj-set-collection / generate-summaries: the collection spreadsheet
# (default "DJ Set Collection"), its scratch tab ("TempClear") and summary
# tab ("Summary_Tab"), the summaries folder under DJ_SETS_FOLDER_ID
# ("Summary"), and where the JSON snapshot is written
# (v1/deejay-sets/deejay_set_collection.json).
# OUTPUT_NAME=
# TEMP_TAB_NAME=
# SUMMARY_TAB_NAME=
# SUMMARY_FOLDER_NAME=
# DEEJAY_SET_COLLECTION_JSON_PATH=
# ── Music tagging ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# retag-music: the folder whose audio files are tagged (default in
# config.py) and files handled per run (default 200; 0 for no cap).
# MUSIC_UPLOAD_SOURCE_FOLDER_ID=
# MAX_UPLOADS_PER_RUN=
# The fingerprint function: the AcoustID key (required there; without it
# every file fails) and the AcoustID score a match must reach before the
# file is written (default 0.90).
# ACOUSTID_API_KEY=
# RETAG_MIN_CONFIDENCE=
# new-music (new music intake): off | dry-run | write (default off; unset or
# unknown is off), its folders (no defaults; with any unset, or two the
# same, the run does nothing), and files per run (default 25; 0 for no cap).
# The state folder holds every music-writing flow's run records, which
# `python -m deejay_cog.music_rollback` reads.
# NEW_MUSIC_MODE=
# NEW_MUSIC_INPUT_FOLDER_ID=
# NEW_MUSIC_DESTINATION_FOLDER_ID=
# NEW_MUSIC_REVIEW_FOLDER_ID=
# NEW_MUSIC_ORIGINALS_FOLDER_ID=
# MUSIC_TAGGING_STATE_FOLDER_ID=
# NEW_MUSIC_MAX_FILES_PER_RUN=
# library-backfill (the library retagged in place, a chunk a run, nightly):
# off | dry-run | write (default off; unset or unknown is off), the
# library's root folder (no default; unset, or the same as the state folder,
# and the run does nothing), files per run (default 10), and Drive file ids
# to pass over, comma-separated (how a file whose audio check fails is
# passed). Its manifest and cursor live in MUSIC_TAGGING_STATE_FOLDER_ID.
# LIBRARY_BACKFILL_MODE=
# LIBRARY_ROOT_FOLDER_ID=
# LIBRARY_BACKFILL_CHUNK_SIZE=
# LIBRARY_BACKFILL_SKIP_FILE_IDS=
# library-scan (files added to and removed from the library reach the
# registry, nightly, before the backfill): off | dry-run | write (default
# off), and the most seconds a run spends listing (default 90).
# LIBRARY_SCAN_MODE=
# LIBRARY_SCAN_LISTING_SECONDS=
# library-identify (unidentified library files identified, linked and
# written with the catalog's values): off | dry-run | write (default off),
# and files tried per run (default 20).
# LIBRARY_IDENTIFY_MODE=
# LIBRARY_IDENTIFY_CHUNK_SIZE=
# library-reconcile (linked files compared with the catalog; a write run
# applies the owner's approvals): off | dry-run | write (default off), and
# files compared per run (default 50).
# LIBRARY_RECONCILE_MODE=
# LIBRARY_RECONCILE_CHUNK_SIZE=
